# XCU shift
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/shift.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.shift.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/positional parameters shall be shifted
class      required
says       shift without an operand moves each positional parameter down by
           one, drops the first, and lowers $# by one.
test       t/001-one.sh

assertion  XCU.shift.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/unsigned decimal integer less than
class      required
says       shift n drops the first n positional parameters; shift 0 changes
           nothing; shifting all of them leaves none and succeeds.
test       t/002-n.sh

assertion  XCU.shift.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/greater than
class      required
says       shift n with n larger than $# returns non-zero (a non-interactive
           shell may exit instead) and, when it goes on, writes a warning to
           standard error.
test       t/003-too-many.sh

assertion  XCU.shift.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/operand is invalid
class      required
says       shift with an operand that is not an unsigned decimal integer
           returns non-zero (or the non-interactive shell exits).
test       t/004-invalid-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.shift.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.5
class      required
says       Inside a function, shift acts on the function's own positional
           parameters; the caller's are restored when the function returns.
test       t/005-function-scope.sh
